### place-service — example requests
# place/place-service-with-loco — "person-style" layout (src/api/rest/).
# Envelope: {"success":bool,"data":...,"error":...} but data/error are
# OMITTED (not null) on the unused side — #[serde(skip_serializing_if)],
# src/api/mod.rs. Different from person/worker/event's "always both keys".
# Gated by PLACE_REQUIRE_AUTH (default off).
#
# GOTCHA (curl-verified): Place has NO #[serde(default)] anywhere, so
# create/match/check-duplicates need the FULL struct — every Vec field
# as [], plus id/created_at/updated_at/is_deleted explicitly. A body with
# only name/address/geo (as a naive reading of the README curl example
# would suggest) fails JSON deserialization. Also: place keeps the
# client-supplied `id` verbatim (never replaces a nil UUID), unlike
# person/worker/event/course — reusing the placeholder id below on a
# second create will 500.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8083
@placeId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health


### Who am I — always requires a valid bearer token, unlike every other
# route in this file (curl-verified: 401 "missing authorization header"
# with none, even though PLACE_REQUIRE_AUTH is off).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/whoami
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Create a place — the full struct (see the GOTCHA note above).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/places
Content-Type: application/json
Accepts-version: 1.0

{
  "id": "{{placeId}}",
  "name": "Central Park",
  "keywords": [],
  "identifiers": [],
  "amenity_features": [],
  "opening_hours": [],
  "is_deleted": false,
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}


### Get the created place back
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/places/{{placeId}}


### Update a place (same full-struct requirement as create)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/places/{{placeId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "{{placeId}}",
  "name": "Central Park (renamed)",
  "keywords": ["park", "landmark"],
  "identifiers": [],
  "amenity_features": [],
  "opening_hours": [],
  "is_deleted": false,
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}


### Search places — total is reported in the JSON body (data.total),
# not response headers, for this crate.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/places/search?q=Central&limit=10


### Probabilistic + deterministic match — also needs the full struct.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/places/match
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "name": "Central Park",
  "keywords": [],
  "identifiers": [],
  "amenity_features": [],
  "opening_hours": [],
  "is_deleted": false,
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}


### Explicit duplicate check (same full-struct body as match)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/places/check-duplicates
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "name": "Central Park",
  "keywords": [],
  "identifiers": [],
  "amenity_features": [],
  "opening_hours": [],
  "is_deleted": false,
  "created_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-01-01T00:00:00Z"
}


### Batch deduplicate — scans the whole index
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/places/deduplicate


### Review queue — list pending candidate pairs
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/places/review-queue?status=pending


### Review queue — decide a pending item
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/places/review-queue/{{reviewId}}/decision
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "status": "confirmed" }


### Merge two confirmed-duplicate places (destructive)
# POST {{baseUrl}}/api/places/merge
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "main_id": "{{placeId}}", "duplicate_id": "<other-uuid>" }


### Masked view (privacy.md)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/places/{{placeId}}/masked


### GDPR export
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/places/{{placeId}}/export


### Audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/places/{{placeId}}/audit


### FHIR R5 — read this place as a Location resource
GET {{baseUrl}}/fhir/Location/{{placeId}}


### Delete (soft-delete) a place
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/places/{{placeId}}
